{"s":"TJX","updated":"2026-11-14T16:43:52.249332+00:00","profile":{"name":"The TJX Companies, Inc.","summary":"The TJX Companies, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates as an off-price apparel and home fashions retailer worldwide. It operates through four segments: Marmaxx, HomeGoods, TJX Canada, and TJX International. The company provides family apparel comprising footwear; accessories, such as beauty and jewelry; home fashion products, including home basics, decorative accessories and giftware, as well as furniture, rugs, lighting, soft home, decorative accessories, tabletop, and cookware; pet and gourmet food; and other merchandise. It also offers home decor, furniture, and seasonal home merchandise. The company sells its products through stores and e-commerce sites. The TJX Companies, Inc. was incorporated in 1962 and is headquartered in Framingham, Massachusetts.","industry":"Apparel Retail","sector":"Consumer Cyclical","employees":377000,"address":"770 Cochituate Road, Framingham, MA 01701, United States","phone":"508 390 1000","website":"https://www.tjx.com","ir":"http://www.tjx.com/investor_landing.asp","exchange":"NYSE","officers":[{"n":"Ms. Carol M. Meyrowitz","t":"Executive Chairman","age":71,"pay":5503632},{"n":"Mr. Ernie L. Herrman","t":"CEO, President & Director","age":64,"pay":10745540},{"n":"Mr. John Klinger","t":"Senior Executive VP & CFO","age":60,"pay":3326376},{"n":"Mr. Kenneth Canestrari","t":"Senior EVP & Group President","age":63,"pay":4212688},{"n":"Mr. Douglas W. Mizzi","t":"Senior EVP & Group President","age":65,"pay":4346800},{"n":"Mr. Bernard Cammarata","t":"Founder & Executive Advisor","age":85,"pay":541929},{"n":"Mr. Jeff Botte","t":"Vice President of Investor Relations"},{"n":"Ms. Alicia C. Kelly","t":"Executive VP, Secretary & General Counsel"},{"n":"Ms. Debra McConnell","t":"Senior Vice President of Global Communications"},{"n":"Peter Benjamin","t":"Senior EVP & Group President","age":62}]},"stats":{"ev":156116516864,"ev_ebit